    "narrative": "The daily optimization for Ghost Ride the WHIP highlights a clear hierarchy of upside, led by **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) and **James Wood** (78.42). **Corbin Carroll** is our primary anchor today against Chandler; the confluence of an elite 5.00 xERA matchup, an advantageous wind blowing out, and a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher that creates a high-probability stolen base environment makes him our most efficient play. **James Wood** follows closely, leveraging his elite 0.425 xwOBA and a prime leadoff spot to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Bieber. **Mickey Moniak** (75.71) also surges into the top tier, benefiting significantly from a 14% dynamic platoon boost and a matchup against King that prioritizes his current hot streak.\n\nSecondary production is anchored by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (65.48) and **Brice Turang** (62.45), both of whom offer reliable returns despite varying conditions. While **Brice Turang** faces a respectable 3.95 xERA arm, his leadoff placement and the wind-out factor keep his efficiency well within the \"Strong\" start tier. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Isaac Paredes** (45.99); despite his sub-50 score, his starting spot is necessitated by internal roster constraints, even as he battles a difficult dynamic platoon disadvantage against Detmers. **Henry Bolte** (56.21) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; while his 10% park factor bump was enticing, his placement in the lower third of the lineup ultimately capped his efficiency relative to the higher-upside options we opted to start. We are monitoring **Dalton Rushing** and **Edwin Arroyo** for any late lineup shifts, as their scores sit right on the periphery of our marginal threshold, though they remain locked in pending further developments.",
